Chunked-prefill probe construction hook (CP-0 prerequisite P1, 2026-08-28).

ONE hunk, one region, two statements of engine change.  All instrumentation
lives in sglang/srt/multiplex/chunk_probe.py and installs itself *by wrapping*
the three PrefillAdder truncation entry points plus Scheduler.run_batch -- and
only when PDMUX_CHUNK_PROBE_PATH is set.  With the variable unset,
maybe_install_chunk_probe returns None immediately, installs nothing, and the
engine keeps running the pristine functions: no added branch anywhere on the
admission path or in run_batch.

WHY HERE AND NOT NEXT TO THE HOLB HOOK.  holb_probe_scheduler_hooks.patch is
mirrored and reverse-applied by
tests/test_holb_probe.py::TestSchedulerHooksInstalled::
test_patch_reapplies_the_hooks_and_nothing_else.  An insertion inside either of
that patch's context windows (the import cluster around
`from sglang.srt.multiplex.holb_probe import ...`, and the block between
`self.grammar_manager = GrammarManager(self)` and `def init_model_config`)
makes the reverse application fail, i.e. it silently costs the holb patch its
reversibility.  The first draft of this patch did exactly that and the existing
test caught it.  This version therefore anchors on
`self.init_deterministic_inference_config()` and imports inside the function so
that the module import cluster is untouched.

The hook must sit after init_cache_with_memory_pool (scheduler.py:397, sets
self.tree_cache) and after init_chunked_prefill (:403, sets
self.chunked_prefill_size, mapping <= 0 to None) because the boot config echo
reads both; the anchor above satisfies that.

--- a/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py
+++ b/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py
@@ -426,6 +426,19 @@
         # Init prefill kv split size when deterministic inference is enabled with various attention backends
         self.init_deterministic_inference_config()
 
+        # Init chunked-prefill probe (arm-agnostic; default OFF).  Returns None
+        # unless PDMUX_CHUNK_PROBE_PATH is set; when set it wraps the three
+        # PrefillAdder truncation entry points plus Scheduler.run_batch, so the
+        # counters live in the scheduler layer and are therefore alive on the
+        # `--chunked-prefill-size -1` arm too -- that arm is the only one whose
+        # prefill runs eager, because cps -1 empties the piecewise CUDA graph
+        # capture list.  Imported here rather than at module scope so this hook
+        # touches exactly one region of the file.
+        # See sglang/srt/multiplex/chunk_probe.py.
+        from sglang.srt.multiplex.chunk_probe import maybe_install_chunk_probe
+
+        self.chunk_probe = maybe_install_chunk_probe(self)
+
         # Init request dispatcher
         self.init_request_dispatcher()
 
